// TEST: build
// BACKENDS: c11, llvm
//
// The one variable allowed to keep an unsized array type without an
// initializer: an `@extern` global.
//
// `@extern` says the storage lives outside the module, so its size is not
// this module's to know — the declaration names the symbol and the element
// type, and the C output is `extern int32_t externTable[];`, which is a
// declaration and not a definition.  The refusals that surround this
// permission are in `unsized.modest`.
//
// Nothing reads the variable: there is no definition to link against, and
// the point here is that the declaration compiles at all.  It went missing
// once: forbidding `[]T` for every variable to catch the local case takes
// this one down with it.

include "libc/ctypes64"


@extern("C")
var externTable: []Int32


func main () -> Int {
	return 0
}
